Hello,

I=E2=80=99m running 3.18.3 (config appended below). With an overlayfs m=
ounted at /root/lower with -olowerdir=3D/root/lower,upperdir=3D/root/up=
per,workdir=3D/root/work, /proc/self/exe points to a path relative to /=
root/lower when a program in /root/lower (before mounting) is run. For =
example, if I put a program named test in /root/lower that prints the r=
esult of readlink on /proc/self/exe, I get /test, whereas if I run the =
same program after unmounting the overlayfs I get /root/lower/test. Is =
this expected behavior?

Thanks,
Shea Levy

